# Repo-root ignores.
#
# `Frontend/.gitignore` covers the application's own build output — node_modules,
# .next, coverage, Playwright results, env files. This file covers what sits
# *beside* it at the root: agent tooling installed into the working copy, and OS
# droppings.
#
# Nothing here is deleted by being listed — these paths stay on disk and keep
# working. They are simply not this repository's source.

# --- Agent tooling (Impeccable) ---
# Installed per working copy, ~140k lines across two near-identical trees, and
# not source for this product. Scoped to the exact directories the installer
# creates rather than to `.claude/` and `.github/` wholesale, because both of
# those are places real project config belongs: a shared `.claude/settings.json`
# and `.github/workflows/` must stay committable.
.claude/skills/
.github/skills/
.github/agents/
.github/hooks/

# Per-developer Claude Code settings. The `.local` suffix is the convention for
# "mine, not the team's" — a shared `.claude/settings.json` is deliberately not
# matched by this.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Impeccable's per-checkout state: hook consent and its scan cache. Previously
# excluded only via `.git/info/exclude`, which lives in one clone and travels to
# nobody — so a teammate saw it as untracked noise. Listed here so the ignore is
# shared.
.impeccable/
**/.impeccable/

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
